WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:09.108
In this video, the agent tests
the app in the browser by itself,

2
00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:13.540
finds a bug, fixes it,
and proves it with shapes that stay.

3
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.770
This is a real run, with the waits sped up.

4
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.843
The prompt asks it to draw a few shapes,
and to fix anything that's broken.

5
00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.842
It picks tools and drags on the canvas in

6
00:00:25.842 --> 00:00:28.258
the integrated browser, like a person would.

7
00:00:28.831 --> 00:00:32.812
One browser action fails, so it
draws with a short script instead.

8
00:00:36.317 --> 00:00:41.715
There it is. A rectangle shows up while
you drag, then vanishes when you let go.

9
00:00:41.715 --> 00:00:45.765
A cleanup check was backwards,
so it threw away real shapes.

10
00:00:51.642 --> 00:00:55.695
After the fix, three rectangles
and an ellipse stay on the canvas.

11
00:00:56.442 --> 00:00:59.841
It ran the build and the
type check, and committed

12
00:00:59.841 --> 00:01:03.240
both changes on the branch,
the label and the fix.

13
00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.532
Nothing was pushed.

14
00:01:10.025 --> 00:01:13.731
Drawing works again, so the next
step starts from a working app.
